<aiml version="2.0">

    <!--
      Pipeline, workflow, case studies, and outcome interpretation. Atomic
      categories, no tables or diagrams in the answer text — these render
      badly inside a chat bubble. Authored follow-ups for every leaf.
    -->

    <category>
        <pattern>HOW DOES THE ANALYSIS PIPELINE WORK</pattern>
        <template><![CDATA[The pipeline has four stages, all running locally:

1. Upload — you point the tool at a Tamarin theory (.spthy).
2. Mutate — for each mutation you ticked, the tool produces one rewritten copy of the theory.
3. Analyse — Tamarin runs against each mutant in turn, producing a verdict (proof, falsification, or timeout).
4. Report — the results come back as a bundle you can compare against the original.

The point is to see how the verdict shifts as the protocol is perturbed — every mutant is one controlled change away from the original.

[[FOLLOWUPS]] What is a mutant? | How are mutants analysed? | How do I read the results?]]></template>
    </category>

    <category><pattern>HOW DOES THE PIPELINE WORK</pattern><template><srai>HOW DOES THE ANALYSIS PIPELINE WORK</srai></template></category>
