    <category>
        <pattern>HOW ARE MUTANTS ANALYSED</pattern>
        <template><![CDATA[Each mutant theory is handed to Tamarin exactly as if you had written it yourself. Tamarin tries to prove every security lemma in the file; for each one it returns:

• Proved — the property still holds after the mutation.
• Falsified — the mutation opened up a concrete attack, and you get the attack trace.
• Timeout — Tamarin gave up before deciding; you can re-run with a higher depth or split the lemma.

The interesting comparisons are usually "Proved on original, Falsified on mutant" — those are the steps or facts that were doing the security work.

[[FOLLOWUPS]] How do I read the results? | What is a mutant? | How does the analysis pipeline work?]]></template>
    </category>

    <category>
        <pattern>HOW DO I READ THE RESULTS</pattern>
        <template><![CDATA[Compare each mutant's verdict to the original's, lemma by lemma:

• Original proved, mutant proved → the mutation made no difference. The step or value being mutated is not security-relevant for that lemma.
• Original proved, mutant falsified → the mutation broke the property. The mutated element is load-bearing — investigate the attack trace.
• Original falsified, mutant proved → unusual; usually means the mutation removed a feature that was itself the attack surface.
• Timeout on either side → not a verdict. Re-run with adjusted depth before drawing conclusions.

For Forget runs, also open the derivation tree to see which alternative paths the agent tried before declaring a block.

[[FOLLOWUPS]] How are mutants analysed? | What is a blocked derivation? | What is Forget?]]></template>
    </category>

    <category><pattern>WHAT DO THE RESULTS MEAN</pattern><template><srai>HOW DO I READ THE RESULTS</srai></template></category>
    <category><pattern>HOW TO INTERPRET RESULTS</pattern><template><srai>HOW DO I READ THE RESULTS</srai></template></category>

    <category>
        <pattern>WHAT FILE FORMAT DO YOU SUPPORT</pattern>
        <template><![CDATA[Tamarin theory files — extension .spthy. The Upload File dialog filters for that extension by default but accepts other files too; if you point it at something Tamarin cannot parse, the mutation step will surface a parse error in the response dialog.

If you have a protocol that is not in Tamarin syntax yet, you will need to convert it first — the tool does not generate Tamarin theories from scratch.

[[FOLLOWUPS]] How do I use this tool? | How does the analysis pipeline work?]]></template>
    </category>

    <category><pattern>WHAT FILES CAN I UPLOAD</pattern><template><srai>WHAT FILE FORMAT DO YOU SUPPORT</srai></template></category>
